4kbas32.bin
-----------

Altair BASIC version 3.2, 4K edition. Written in 1975 by Bill Gates,
Paul Allen and Monte Davidoff for MITS, and published by MITS for the
Altair 8800.

  Size   4096 bytes
  MD5    8e6f8daa63a8b8b64b26fe36a33bfb95
  SHA1   6e0d2347a30af5a8b9546a14ddd123e5b46646a4
  Load   absolute at 0000H, no boot loader needed

Only 0000H-0EFAH (3835 bytes) is program; the rest of the file is zero
padding up to 4 KB, which becomes BASIC's own workspace.

The copyright in this program is Microsoft's. It has never been
formally released, and no licence to redistribute it has been granted.
It is included here on the same footing as the many other Altair
simulators and preservation archives that carry it: as a historical
artifact, for study and for running on a simulator of the machine it
was written for. If you are the rights holder and would rather it were
not here, please open an issue on the repository and it will be
removed.

The identical file - byte for byte - can be obtained from:

  https://s2js.com/altair/4kbas32.bin
  https://github.com/companje/Altair8800  (data/4kbas32.bin)

A near-complete annotated disassembly of this exact version is at
http://altairbasic.org, which is the best place to start if you want to
know how it works.

If you would rather not have this file in your copy of the repository,
delete it. The simulator's Load 4K BASIC button will simply report that
it is missing, and Load Binary File will still load a copy you supply
yourself.
